    id:'js-001', title:'What is JavaScript?', level:'L1', subtopic:'Fundamentals',
    what:'JavaScript is a dynamically typed, garbage-collected programming language used to add behavior to web applications and also to build servers, tooling, and other applications through runtimes such as Node.js.',
    how:'A JavaScript engine parses source code, creates an internal representation, optimizes hot code, and executes it. In a browser, JavaScript also interacts with Web APIs such as the DOM, timers, and fetch; those APIs are provided by the host environment, not by the language itself.',
    code:`const user = { name: 'Barani' };\nconsole.log(user.name);`,
